            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="RIT01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Joseph</forename>
                        <surname>Ritson</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1752-10-02">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1803-09-23"/>
                    <occupation>antiquary</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>There is a well-documented friendship between Godwin and Joseph Ritson - see, for example, St Clair. 
  Godwin's 1796 list identifies his first contact in 1793 and there is regular contact until Ritson's death ten years later.</p>
                        <p>Godwin records writing his 'Life of Ritson' on 26 October 1803, just over a month after Ritson's death: 'Character of Ritson, 4 1/2 pages'. The Life
    was published in the Monthly Magazine in November 1803 and later republished in the Monthly Mirror in May 1805.
    There are two copies of the manuscript in the Abinger collection. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS Abinger c. 55, fols. 75-80: [26 October 1803]</bibl>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS Abinger c. 22, fols. 168-71: [26 October 1803]</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
